#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# polynomial_quotient

#% text
# `polynomial_quotient(p, q, x)` gives the quotient of the division of `p` by `q` as polynomials in `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The division is with remainder: `p == q*polynomial_quotient(p, q, x) + polynomial_remainder(p, q, x)`, with the remainder of lower degree in `x` than `q`. Coefficients may be rational functions of other symbols.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
polynomial_quotient(x^3 + 2*x + 1, x - 1, x)
#% output
#= 3 + x + x^2

#% cell
polynomial_quotient(x^4 - 1, x^2 + 1, x)
#% output
#= -1 + x^2

#% cell
polynomial_quotient(x^2, 2*x + 1, x)
#% output
#= -1/4 + (1/2)*x

#% cell
polynomial_quotient(x^2 + a*x, x + b, x)
#% output
#= a + x - b

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The division identity:

#% cell
p = x^5 + 3*x^2 - 1; q = x^2 - x + 2; expand(q*polynomial_quotient(p, q, x) + polynomial_remainder(p, q, x) - p)
#% output
#= 0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `polynomial_remainder`, `polynomial_gcd`, `apart`
